From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mini-code benchmarks <benchmarks@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:01:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] singularity: build a task's .sif from its Dockerfile

Terminal-Bench 2 tasks ship environment/Dockerfile, not the docker_image that
the Singularity environment required, so every task failed validation before a
container existed.

- derive a content-addressed image name from the Dockerfile (harbor-local/<task>:<sha>)
  and build it with `apptainer build --fakeroot`, cached under the image cache dir
- report a fakeroot refusal as such instead of an opaque build failure
- use apptainer when installed (HARBOR_CONTAINER_BIN overrides), and pass
  --force to pull so a stale cache cannot produce an invalid .sif
- default --no-mount to home,tmp: 'bind-paths' also suppressed the /etc/resolv.conf
  bind, leaving the container without DNS (apt/curl in the verifier failed)
- bootstrap.sh: use a pre-baked /opt/harbor-server venv when the image ships one,
  find python3 on PATH, and stop apt's sandbox from rejecting the fakeroot user

Tested with a real task (gpt2-codegolf): the SIF is built from the Dockerfile and
the FastAPI server boots inside it.
